# defaults-runtime.config — `M189c`: `C93`'s run-time leg (`config:directive:defaults`).
#
# `C93`'s other four legs are `tflw check` legs, and `tflw check` reads `defaults` through the
# checker's own merge. The runtime has a second merge (`resolve.ts`), and a hand mutation of that
# one — `defaults` applied to the default env only — left every `check` leg green on the box on
# 2026-09-13, because none of them runs anything. This config is the leg that does: one `header`
# line in `defaults`, two envs pointing at the same arrival server, and the plant runs `--env two`,
# the NON-default env, and reads the header back off the wire. A build that merged `defaults` into
# the default env alone answers with two arrivals carrying nothing.

defaults
  header "X-Def" is "c93-shared"

env one default
  api "http://127.0.0.1:4507/base"

env two
  api "http://127.0.0.1:4507/base"
